lines+=['', 'All main outputs are generated from native values through the fixed C16 port. Complete correctness requires the emitted byte and own EOS within four decisions. METRICS.csv includes every INITIAL/OLD8/OLD16/NEW4/FINAL/REST128 panel, teacher-prefix payload/EOS accuracy, bits/target, empty EOS and CAP. REST128 is128*DELTA native seconds, not128 whole records.','', '## Frozen gates and representation measurements','', '| World | Δ final total | Δ NEW | Δ conditional retention | OLD×NEW Jaccard drop | LPS OLD8→OLD16 stability | Changed OLD16 codes /80 | P1 | P2 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|']
for w in s['worlds']:
 l=w['arms']['LPS-16'];rr='undefined' if w['delta_R'] is None else f"{w['delta_R']:.4f}"
 lines.append(f"| {w['world']} | {w['delta_total']:+d} | {w['delta_NEW']:+d} | {rr} | {w['J_drop']:.6f} | {l['S']:.6f} | {l['changed_codes_OLD16']} | {w['P1']} | {w['P2']} |")
lines+=['',f"P3 technical/resource gate: **{s['P3']}**. P1 requires≥8 additional complete final items in each world, NEW loss≤2, and conditional OLD retention decrease≤.05. P2 requires Jaccard drop≥.05 in each world, stability≥.85, a real code change and no new final contradictory duplicate codes. These are fixed engineering screens, not p-values; they were not loosened after outcomes.",'', 'The initial evaluator-only code lookup recalls80/80 and the position-frequency floor5/80 in both worlds. Exact-key lookup can solve this fixture. The learner never receives lookup tables. Initial and measured per-side KC population counts agree between arms; inhibitory competition changes identity rather than sparseness. All final conflicting-code counts are in SUMMARY.json. A low Jaccard value alone is not proof of reduced synaptic interference.','', '## Matched write interventions','', '| World | Arm | Mean OLD sentinel margin damage | Shadow events |','|---|---|---:|---:|']
for w in s['worlds']:
 for arm,r in w['arms'].items():lines.append(f"| {w['world']} | {arm} | {r['D']:.6f} | 8 |")
lines+=['', 'Damage is zero-write minus written mean teacher-prefix target margin across eight prespecified OLD sentinels; positive means harm. At the first NEW pass, record ordinals1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15 in each arm/world receive separately charged shadow interventions at the payload target. Each pair uses identical source state, teacher time, KC code and prospective read condition. Zero writes include actual native passive decay. Shadows do not enter the live learner or update L. Delivered logit displacement and self-target effects are saved with each intervention. This is a write intervention diagnostic, not a causal mediation proof for Jaccard.','', '## Three cycles and preserved failures','', '1. **C0 design/feasibility:** remote V175 design and WCFI native source pinned; opaque generator port, gamma, topology, task ceiling/floor, gates and clocks fixed. Both fresh-world initial feasibility tests pass.','2. **C1 technical/revision:** original native parity and zero-L parity passed. A checker mistakenly demanded a code change for every arbitrary nonzero-L fixture; it stopped after8 technical records. R1 replaced only that assertion with independent scalar edge-sum/TopK parity. A continuation-dispatch error then stopped with zero extra observations. Both failures, original sources and costs are preserved. Remaining checks continued without replaying those8 records; total18 technical records/34 targets. Gamma, candidate equations and main gates were not tuned.','3. **C2 fixed development/audit:** two fresh worlds×two independent matched births×1152 records; six fixed panels and32 same-state NEW interventions. A separate saved-only reducer checks all published arithmetic, hashes, exposure counters, clocks, KC populations, correct sets, code stability and original gates. No model was rerun for reporting.','', 'The technical source audit is separately implemented AST/structure verification, not an independent human review. It verifies a cue-only update function with no answer, task, phase or item-ID argument. The first-answer raw cue trace is cached before its target; L stays fixed throughout the record and updates only after observed EOS. Read-only panels freeze all persistent state. Different technical answer labels yield the same L update. Inhibited observed records update L while native values undergo passive events.','', '## Exposure, resources and implementation limits','',f"Main **4608 full records /9216 expected targets**, four correlated-within-life histories; technical18/34; combined **4626 full records /9250 targets**, plus66 partial shadow targets and2436 own/TF probe pairs. Counts include reference and passive technical presentations. No replay, arithmetic training, E3 decision, extra world or main restart occurred.",'',f"Cumulative worker CPU: **{s['CPU']:.2f}s** ({s['CPU']/3600:.4f}CPU-h); peak RSS across attempts: {s['peak_RSS_bytes']/2**20:.1f}MiB. Saved-only reduction adds {a['reducer_CPU']:.3f}s. One worker/one numerical thread; caffeinate followed each active worker and ended on exit. The1.5x preflight forecast was755.4CPU-s against7200s allowed. All failed technical attempts remain charged.",'', '| World | Arm | Total measured CPU including probes | Training-call CPU including embedded shadow diagnostics |','|---|---|---:|---:|']
for w in s['worlds']:
 for arm,r in w['arms'].items():lines.append(f"| {w['world']} | {arm} | {r['life_total_CPU']:.3f} | {r['life_train_CPU_including_shadow']:.3f} |")
lines+=['',f"The fixed graph has{q['graph_edges']} undirected same-side edges. Mutable L uses{q['L_bytes']}bytes; endpoint arrays use{q['topology_bytes']}bytes. Encoding retains global native projection/top-k sorting, adds a second per-side sort and scans the fixed edge set; L decay/update also scans all edges per completed record. This is local in learning dependencies, not a demonstrated scalable sparse-work implementation. Counted inhibition edge visits: {c['counts']['inhibition_edge_visits']:,}; update edge visits: {c['counts']['lateral_update_edge_visits']:,}; additional cloned L bytes: {c['counts']['lateral_clone_bytes']:,}. Wrapper clone traffic excludes some inherited internal native copies.",'', 'The training-call timer includes shadow callbacks, so it must not be described as a clean production-step benchmark. The per-life total includes all prescribed diagnostics. Accuracy bought with extra computation is not automatically sample/compute superiority. Fixed-gain DELTA is identical between arms, but changed encoding can alter actual delivered functional strength; measured shadow d is reported rather than assuming a pure geometry-only intervention.','', '## Evidence boundary and next decision','', 'The result applies to this inhibition-circuit package against BASE. There is no strength-matched frozen-inhibition arm, so even a pass would not isolate learned plasticity from adding inhibition itself. Two randomized worlds share canonical wiring and do not support general architecture claims or item-bootstrap-as-world confidence intervals. OLD and NEW are directly reinforced opaque associations; this is recitation-compatible E1. The actual long-term goal remains learned reusable information, with unseen addition as an independently prospective diagnostic.','', 'See REVISED_DESIGN.md for the evidence-based next step. Preserve gradual warmup, local rules, native byte/EOS output, no attention/Transformers/ELM and no task-specific structure. No follow-up run or adoption is automatic. Raw states, full output panels, KC codes and historical failed attempts remain local; published aggregate summaries must not be mistaken for complete raw replication assets.']
(H/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
# Revision preserves the registered treatment and failed gates; it does not launch a rescue.
r=['# V175-R1 — post-cycle interpretation and revised next decision','', 'The R1 technical amendment corrects an overstrong measurement assertion. It changes neither the V175 learner nor its original main screens. All original sources and failed-attempt artifacts remain preserved.','',f"Completed outcome: **{s['verdict']}**. All four main lives finished under the authorized budget.",'']
for w in s['worlds']:
 b=w['arms']['BASE'];l=w['arms']['LPS-16'];r.append(f"- World {w['world']}: final complete answers BASE{b['T']}/80 vs LPS{l['T']}/80 (delta{w['delta_total']:+d}); OLD{b['O1']} vs{l['O1']}; NEW{b['N1']} vs{l['N1']}. Jaccard drop{w['J_drop']:.6f}, address stability{l['S']:.6f}; P1={w['P1']}, P2={w['P2']}.")
r+=['', 'The circuit was not simply inactive: all80 measured OLD-boundary codes changed in each world, while address stability remained above0.97. The specific failure is weak overlap reduction and no consistent capability benefit, not an inability to execute local plasticity. Shadow OLD margin damage was higher under LPS in both world-level means; this is descriptive and does not establish a mediation pathway.','', '## What to retain','', 'The native writer, gradual warmup and own-byte/EOS endpoint remain the operative baseline. Nonzero inhibition does not have to change every individual input code; technical correctness is established by independent formula parity and population counts. Mechanism activity is measured separately on actual learned main states. The original requirement of some nonzero learned code change remains in P2.','', 'Do not equate learning a local coactivity trace with learning useful pattern separation. Report whether codes actually moved, whether OLD/NEW overlap decreased, whether existing addresses drifted, and whether complete answers improved. These are distinct results. Do not reduce the0.05 overlap screen or8-item capability screen after observing a near miss. They are operational screens, not mathematical impossibility boundaries.','', '## Next prospective design','']
if all(w['P1'] and w['P2'] for w in s['worlds']):
 r+=['A separate fixed-inhibition and matched-compute control is warranted before confirmation. Freeze this exact candidate and data-generation rule on fresh worlds; compare plastic inhibition against an outcome-independent fixed inhibitory circuit with matched measured strength. Preserve observed-write-inhibited controls so representation drift and value-write effects can be separated. Do not call V175 a confirmed core or E3 transfer.']
else:
 r+=['Do not adopt or automatically retune LPS-16-D1. This exact sparse one-pass cue-coactivity rule did not pass the complete registered development screen. A failure here is not a family-wide impossibility result for inhibitory circuits.','', 'The next useful contrast should localize value-write protection versus address movement on the existing native substrate. Prefer one generic local fast/slow consolidation/protection candidate with the calibrated writer held fixed, rather than adding replay, a different gamma, more neighbors or more rounds to this opened experiment. Any new coefficient, connectivity or learning-rule change needs a prospective design and fresh worlds. The circuit must learn its protection signal only from local activity and genuine past feedback, never OLD/NEW IDs, expected future outputs or arithmetic structure.','', 'A prospective test should retain writer-enabled versus inhibited observations with exactly matched clocks, and include a correction phase so protection cannot win by permanently freezing all earlier associations. If instead inhibition is pursued, first use an independent unlabeled technical fixture to establish that the proposed circuit meaningfully changes the relevant address overlaps at bounded cost; that is engineering calibration, not a new efficacy claim on V175 worlds. Keep a frozen-inhibition comparator to distinguish the circuit’s static conditioning from its plasticity.']
r+=['', '## Limits retained','', 'Only E0/E1/E1-R were tested. Exact-key lookup can solve every scored association. No unseen addition, E3, broad language learning or core adoption was established. Keep gradual warmup, local rules and native byte/EOS output; no attention/Transformers/ELM, arithmetic features, task-specific model circuitry or external answer decoder. No follow-up is launched by this document.','', 'Source/metadata discipline for a future run should capture phase runtime and calibration artifact hashes explicitly before admission, record embedded shadow cost separately from live teaching cost, and preserve failed partial states before assertions. This report does not retrofit a production-efficiency claim onto instrumentation-heavy development code.']
